= Availability heuristic — Technical =

== Accessibility cue ==
A stylized model is:

<pre>
judged frequency/probability
= f(retrieved content, retrieval ease, task information)
</pre>

Availability need not dominate when explicit statistical information is trusted and usable.

== Bias sources ==
Accessibility can be distorted by:

* media exposure;
* emotional intensity;
* recency;
* distinctiveness;
* retrievability;
* imaginability;
* personal experience.

== Ease-of-retrieval dissociation ==
Manipulations that make recall subjectively difficult can reduce judged frequency even when more examples are actually generated.

This supports a distinction between retrieved content and the metacognitive experience of retrieval.

== Ecological value ==
Availability can be adaptive when memory accessibility is correlated with environmental frequency or relevance.

The heuristic is not intrinsically irrational.

== References ==
* Tversky & Kahneman (1973, 1974).
* Schwarz and ease-of-retrieval research.
